avid Crowley faces congressman Tom Tiffany in a state that sits right at even partisan balance. Polling since August has been remarkably steady, with every survey — including those sponsored by Republican-leaning firms — showing Crowley ahead by three to five points among likely voters. The most recent polls from late September and early October show the same pattern.\n\nTiffany holds a major financial advantage, raising nearly $11 million to Crowley's $1 million, and his advertising could still shift the race. But prediction markets put Crowley's chances near 80%, and several expert raters lean Democratic even as others call it a tossup. The race remains competitive, with Fox Valley swing voters and local issues like data centers and jail policies in play, but the evidence favors Crowley by a modest margin.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.7127, "margin": 2.83}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.7543, "margin": 3.5}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.7549, "margin": 3.5}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.7725, "margin": 3.8}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.7589, "margin": 4.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.7208, "margin": 3.5}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.724, "margin": 3.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.7645, "margin": 3.5}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.7536, "margin": 3.5}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.7419, "margin": 3.2}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.746, "margin": 3.2}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.7525, "margin": 3.2}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.7388, "margin": 3.0}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.6631, "margin": 2.5}, {"date": "2026-10-06", "p_dem": 0.6796, "margin": 2.7}, {"date": "2026-10-07", "p_dem": 0.6642, "margin": 2.5}, {"date": "2026-10-08", "p_dem": 0.7316, "margin": 3.2}, {"date": "2026-10-09", "p_dem": 0.696, "margin": 3.0}, {"date": "2026-10-10", "p_dem": 0.7094, "margin": 3.0}, {"date": "2026-10-11", "p_dem": 0.7399, "margin": 3.5}, {"date": "2026-10-12", "p_dem": 0.7761, "margin"